// Title: book/src/stdlib/sys/io.md says a wrong-direction stream call is an
// IOError at run time and lists sys::process::Pipe / sys::io::Stdio; both are gone.
// Command: graphix --check book-modules-udt-io-direction.gx
// Expected (per io.md "Which stream implements what"): compiles, the write
//   returns an `IOError at run time.
// Observed: refused at compile time: "Stdin does not implement Write".
//   process.gxi / io.gxi declare ChildStdin/ChildStdout/ChildStderr and
//   Stdin/Stdout/Stderr; no type Pipe or Stdio exists.
use sys::io::{Write};
Write::write_exact(sys::io::stdin(null), buffer::from_string("x"))
